# Styling (NativeWind)

- NativeWind 4.2 on Tailwind 3.4 is the only styling method. `tailwind.config.js` sets `colors`, `spacing`, `borderRadius`, `borderWidth`, `opacity`, `fontSize` from `src/shared/theme/tokens.ts` without `extend`; only `minHeight.touch` and `minWidth.touch` extend.
- `tokens.ts` is the single source for JS too: navigation theme, `ActivityIndicator` color, `android_ripple`, image sizes, through `@shared/theme`.
- `className` for static styles with token classes only: `bg-canvas`, `text-ink`, `p-lg`, `rounded-md`, `min-h-touch`.
- `style` only for runtime values (safe-area insets, screen width), passed as a memoized variable; never an inline object or array.
- Variants are module-level typed class maps: `Record<Variant, string>` with `as const satisfies`.
- Conditional classes through `clsx`; no interpolated class names.
- No arbitrary values in square brackets, no color literals outside `tokens.ts`, no `StyleSheet`.
- The favorite highlight is `bg-favorite border-favorite-outline` plus the "In favorites" badge from the `posts-list` widget.
- A new visual value means a new token, never a one-off class. Restart Metro with `--reset-cache` after token or config changes.

Checks:
- `react-native/no-inline-styles`, `react-native/no-color-literals`, eslint-plugin-tailwindcss `no-custom-classname`, `no-arbitrary-value`, `no-contradicting-classname`, `classnames-order` (enabled). Strings inside class maps are not linted; review them.
- ESLint `no-restricted-syntax` for literal `style` and `*Style` values, color strings outside `tokens.ts` and interpolated classes; `no-restricted-imports` for `StyleSheet` (enabled).

Full guide: @docs/ai/guidelines/styling.md
